@startuml
title SplitSmart Component Architecture (Distinct MVP and complete product; proposed)
left to right direction

package "A. Java Swing MVP (proposed)" {
  [Swing desktop presentation] as SwingUI
  [GUI-independent application services] as MvpApp
  [Domain rules\nexpense, approval, money, balance] as MvpDomain
  [Persistence adapter] as MvpStore
  [In-app notification inbox] as MvpNotify
  [Receipt storage adapter] as MvpReceipt
  [JUnit 5 tests] as MvpTests

  SwingUI --> MvpApp
  MvpApp --> MvpDomain
  MvpApp --> MvpStore
  MvpApp --> MvpNotify
  MvpApp --> MvpReceipt
  MvpTests ..> MvpDomain
  MvpTests ..> MvpApp
}

package "B. Complete customer product (separate future delivery)" {
  [Web client] as Web
  [Android client] as Android
  [iOS client] as IOS
  [Authenticated versioned API] as API
  [Shared domain and application services] as SharedDomain
  [Identity integration] as Identity
  [Transactional data store] as ProductStore
  [Private receipt store] as ProductReceipt
  [Notification adapters] as ProductNotify
  [Authorized report queries] as ProductReports

  Web --> API
  Android --> API
  IOS --> API
  API --> SharedDomain
  SharedDomain --> Identity
  SharedDomain --> ProductStore
  SharedDomain --> ProductReceipt
  SharedDomain --> ProductNotify
  SharedDomain --> ProductReports
}

note bottom
  No components shown here are verified as implemented. The MVP's shared-service
  boundary is needed only if multi-user collaboration is in MVP scope. Do not infer
  shared source code or that Swing fulfills web, Android, or iOS requirements.
end note
@enduml
